# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# Supplier drops are committed extracted, for provenance — the manifest,
# size map, prompts and contact sheet are the record of where the artwork
# came from, and they are small. What is excluded is everything that would
# be a second copy of bytes already in the repo: the archive itself, and the
# drop's own `images/` folder, which is byte-for-byte what now lives in
# public/images/nsrl/ and is the copy the site actually serves.
assets/*.zip
assets/NSRL-All-29-Image-Replacements/NSRL-Image-Replacements/images/
# Same rule for the redesign kit: its briefs, manifest, CSVs, SVGs, demo and
# component are the record and are committed. Its three source PNGs are not —
# public/images/editorial/ holds the same pixels as WebP at the identical
# native dimensions, and that is the copy the site serves.
assets/NSRL_Redesign_Kit/assets/*.png

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
